            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-27983-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-27983 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attacker can make the Node.js HTTP/2 server completely unavailable by sending a small amount of HTTP/2 frames packets with a few HTTP/2 frames inside. It is possible to leave some data in nghttp2 memory after reset when headers with HTTP/2 CONTINUATION frame are sent to the server and then a TCP connection is abruptly closed by the client triggering the Http2Session destructor while header frames are still being processed (and stored in memory) causing a race condition."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-27983\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 18.20.1,20.12.1,21.7.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-27983](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-27983)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-27983**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 10.8.0  | 18.20.1,20.12.1,21.7.2  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-27983](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-27983)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/node@10.8.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
