                "text": "Some HTTP/2 implementations are vulnerable to unconstrained interal data buffering, potentially leading to a denial of service. The attacker opens the HTTP/2 window so the peer can send without constraint; however, they leave the TCP window closed so the peer cannot actually write (many of) the bytes on the wire. The attacker then sends a stream of requests for a large response object. Depending on how the servers queue the responses, this can consume excess memory, CPU, or both."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-9517\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 12.8.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2019-9517](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-9517)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-9517**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 10.8.0  | 12.8.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2019-9517](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-9517)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/node@10.8.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
