              "id": "CVE-2025-23166-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-23166 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The C++ method SignTraits::DeriveBits() may incorrectly call ThrowException() based on user-supplied inputs when executing in a background thread, crashing the Node.js process. Such cryptographic operations are commonly applied to untrusted inputs. Thus, this mechanism potentially allows an adversary to remotely crash a Node.js runtime."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-23166\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 20.19.2,22.15.1,23.11.1,24.0.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-23166](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23166)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-23166**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 10.8.0  | 20.19.2,22.15.1,23.11.1,24.0.2  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-23166](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23166)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/node@10.8.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
