            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-44533-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-44533 medium vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Node.js \u003c 12.22.9, \u003c 14.18.3, \u003c 16.13.2, and \u003c 17.3.1 did not handle multi-value Relative Distinguished Names correctly. Attackers could craft certificate subjects containing a single-value Relative Distinguished Name that would be interpreted as a multi-value Relative Distinguished Name, for example, in order to inject a Common Name that would allow bypassing the certificate subject verification.Affected versions of Node.js that do not accept multi-value Relative Distinguished Names and are thus not vulnerable to such attacks themselves. However, third-party code that uses node's ambiguous presentation of certificate subjects may be vulnerable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-44533\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 12.22.9,14.18.3,16.13.2,17.3.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2021-44533](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-44533)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-44533**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | node  | 10.8.0  | 12.22.9,14.18.3,16.13.2,17.3.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2021-44533](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-44533)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/node@10.8.0"
