            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-21717-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-21717 medium vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in V8's string hashing mechanism causes integer-like strings to be hashed to their numeric value, making hash collisions trivially predictable. By crafting a request that causes many such collisions in V8's internal string table, an attacker can significantly degrade performance of the Node.js process.\r\n\r\nThe most common trigger is any endpoint that calls `JSON.parse()` on attacker-controlled input, as JSON parsing automatically internalizes short strings into the affected hash table.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability affects **20.x, 22.x, 24.x, and 25.x**."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-21717\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 20.20.2,22.22.2,24.14.1,25.8.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-21717](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-21717)",
