            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-21715-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-21715 low vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in Node.js Permission Model filesystem enforcement leaves `fs.realpathSync.native()` without the required read permission checks, while all comparable filesystem functions correctly enforce them.\r\n\r\nAs a result, code running under `--permission` with restricted `--allow-fs-read` can still use `fs.realpathSync.native()` to check file existence, resolve symlink targets, and enumerate filesystem paths outside of permitted directories.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability affects **20.x, 22.x, 24.x, and 25.x** processes using the Permission Model where `--allow-fs-read` is intentionally restricted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-21715\nSeverity: low\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 20.20.2,22.22.2,24.14.1,25.8.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-21715](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-21715)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-21715**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | node  | 10.8.0  | 20.20.2,22.22.2,24.14.1,25.8.2  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-21715](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-21715)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/node@10.8.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-21716-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-21716 low vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An incomplete fix for CVE-2024-36137 leaves `FileHandle.chmod()` and `FileHandle.chown()` in the promises API without the required permission checks, while their callback-based equivalents (`fs.fchmod()`, `fs.fchown()`) were correctly patched.\r\n\r\nAs a result, code running under `--permission` with restricted `--allow-fs-write` can still use promise-based `FileHandle` methods to modify file permissions and ownership on already-open file descriptors, bypassing the intended write restrictions.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability affects **20.x, 22.x, 24.x, and 25.x** processes using the Permission Model where `--allow-fs-write` is intentionally restricted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-21716\nSeverity: low\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 20.20.2,22.22.2,24.14.1,25.8.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-21716](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-21716)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-21716**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | node  | 10.8.0  | 20.20.2,22.22.2,24.14.1,25.8.2  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-21716](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-21716)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
